Upstream sources
================

Every face under packaging/fonts/truetype/ comes from the release named here and
is an unmodified member of the archive named with it. A sha256 is of the archive
as downloaded from the upstream project's own release page, not of the extracted
face; `sha256sum` the archive again to check it.

Each family's OFL.txt is that family's own licence file, copied byte for byte.
They are not interchangeable: the copyright notice and the Reserved Font Names
are stated in the file, and they differ per family.


truetype/source-code-pro/
-------------------------

Project   https://github.com/adobe-fonts/source-code-pro
Release   2.042R-u/1.062R-i/1.026R-vf. Upright and italic are versioned apart:
          `fc-query -f '%{fontversion}' <face>` reports 2.042 for Regular and
          Bold, 1.062 for It and BoldIt.
Archive   TTF-source-code-pro-2.042R-u_1.062R-i.zip
          sha256 0c85bac90d15c040b82939aa92bc8404420fccc02e37bbcb9c93a7f21abb52c6
Faces     TTF/SourceCodePro-{Regular,Bold,It,BoldIt}.ttf
Family    Source Code Pro
Licence   The TTF archive of this release carries no licence file, so OFL.txt is
          LICENSE.md from the repository at the same tag:
          https://github.com/adobe-fonts/source-code-pro
          sha256 7c940e28a5388e9bba866cf0e408edda45fe0899ba98665b8f6ab31dc5e4b8ff
          That checksum is of the licence file itself, which is stable, rather
          than of a generated tag archive, which is not.

The release also ships ExtraLight, Light, Medium, Semibold and Black, each with
an italic, and the variable fonts. Only the four faces above are shipped: the
package promises Regular, Bold, Italic and BoldItalic in every family, and a
weight a caller has to name by family string is a second promise.


